<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Bushehr</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1850 CE (approx.) · capital Bushehr</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Arab-ruled port state on the Persian Gulf coast, under the Al Madhkur sheikhs, that became Iran's main harbour and briefly held Bahrain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a> as a naval base in the 1730s. After his death in 1747, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-madhkur">Al Madhkur</a>, an Arab family settled on the Persian coast, ruled the port as hereditary sheikhs. Sheikh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasr-al-madhkur">Nasir Al Madhkur</a> extended their power across the Gulf, taking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> in 1753.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a> became the main port of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the Gulf. In 1763 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zand-empire">Zand Empire</a> and the sheikh allowed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> to open a factory there, and it later became the seat of the British Political Resident in the Gulf. The sheikhs combined trade, customs revenue and a small fleet, paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> rulers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-madhkur">Al Madhkur</a> lost <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> to the Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> in 1783. Under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran</a> their authority was steadily reduced, and by about 1850 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a> was governed by appointed officials.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1750 CE – 1850 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.53%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bushehr</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nasir Al Madhkur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Al Madhkur of Bushehr, Bushire sheikhdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1800&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-bushehr" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Bushehr on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6007 1118 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Bushehr lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6327 1374L6364 1269M6327 1374L6298 1144"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6364 1269h0M6298 1144h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6327 1374h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6327 1374h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bushehr. <a href="/atlas?year=1800&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-bushehr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
